= Zero-knowledge proof — Simple =

A zero-knowledge proof lets a prover demonstrate that a statement is true without revealing the secret information used to prove it. That does not automatically make the whole application anonymous or private.

'''Important boundary:''' zero-knowledge proof ≠ encryption.

